Relevant columns, their possible usage, and typical conditions  
•  "FORUMTOPICS"."FirstForumMessageId": links every topic to the very first forum‑message.  \
  Condition — IS NOT NULL.  
•  "FORUMMESSAGES"."Id": matches the message id coming from "FirstForumMessageId".  
•  "FORUMMESSAGES"."PostUserId": the author of that first message.  
•  "FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"."ForumMessageId": id of the voted message.  
•  "FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"."FromUserId": voter → DISTINCT count of these per message = message‑score.  
•  "USERS"."UserName": printable user name for the author.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake queries (each limited to 20 rows) that gradually build the required result.  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes and each statement is annotated.

```sql
-- 1) Inspect forum topics and the column that stores the id of the first message
SELECT 
  "Id"                        AS "TopicId",
  "FirstForumMessageId"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS"
WHERE "FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Bring in the real message row for those first‑message ids
SELECT 
  t."FirstForumMessageId",
  m."PostUserId",
  m."PostDate",
  m."Message"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS"   t
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES" m
      ON m."Id" = t."FirstForumMessageId"
WHERE t."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Look at the raw vote rows for any one first message
SELECT 
  v."Id"                  AS "VoteId",
  v."ForumMessageId",
  v."FromUserId",
  v."VoteDate"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
WHERE v."ForumMessageId" IN (
      SELECT "FirstForumMessageId"
      FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS"
      WHERE "FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
      LIMIT 1)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Compute message‑score (distinct voters) for each first message
SELECT 
  v."ForumMessageId",
  COUNT(DISTINCT v."FromUserId") AS "MessageScore"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS" t
      ON t."FirstForumMessageId" = v."ForumMessageId"
GROUP BY v."ForumMessageId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Average message‑score over ALL first messages
WITH scores AS (
  SELECT 
    v."ForumMessageId",
    COUNT(DISTINCT v."FromUserId") AS "MessageScore"
  FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
  JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS" t
        ON t."FirstForumMessageId" = v."ForumMessageId"
  GROUP BY v."ForumMessageId"
)
SELECT AVG("MessageScore") AS "AvgFirstMsgScore"
FROM scores;
```

```sql
-- 6) Combine author, score, and the difference from the global average (all first messages)
WITH scores AS (
  SELECT 
    v."ForumMessageId",
    COUNT(DISTINCT v."FromUserId") AS "MessageScore"
  FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
  JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS" t
        ON t."FirstForumMessageId" = v."ForumMessageId"
  GROUP BY v."ForumMessageId"
),
avg_score AS (
  SELECT AVG("MessageScore") AS "AvgScore" FROM scores
)
SELECT 
  m."PostUserId",
  s."MessageScore",
  ABS(s."MessageScore" - a."AvgScore") AS "AbsDiffFromAvg"
FROM scores                 s
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES" m
      ON m."Id" = s."ForumMessageId"
CROSS JOIN avg_score        a
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) If a user authored several first messages, keep only their best‑scoring one
WITH scores AS (
  SELECT 
    v."ForumMessageId",
    COUNT(DISTINCT v."FromUserId") AS "MessageScore"
  FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
  JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS" t
        ON t."FirstForumMessageId" = v."ForumMessageId"
  GROUP BY v."ForumMessageId"
),
msg_plus_author AS (
  SELECT 
    m."PostUserId",
    s."MessageScore"
  FROM scores s
  JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES" m
        ON m."Id" = s."ForumMessageId"
),
best_per_user AS (
  SELECT 
    "PostUserId",
    MAX("MessageScore") AS "BestMessageScore"
  FROM msg_plus_author
  GROUP BY "PostUserId"
)
SELECT * FROM best_per_user
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Attach usernames to those best scores
WITH best_per_user AS (
  SELECT 
    m."PostUserId",
    MAX(COUNT(DISTINCT v."FromUserId")) AS "BestMessageScore"
  FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES" v
  JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMTOPICS"      t ON t."FirstForumMessageId" = v."ForumMessageId"
  JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGES"    m ON m."Id" = v."ForumMessageId"
  GROUP BY m."PostUserId", v."ForumMessageId"
)
SELECT 
  u."UserName",
  b."BestMessageScore"
FROM best_per_user b
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS" u
      ON u."Id" = b."PostUserId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
